  "question": {
    "text": "Let a vertical tower <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;have its end&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;on the level ground. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> be the mid-point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be a point on the ground such that&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#8736;</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></math> is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
